  "implementationGuidance": [
    "Keep generic feedback.Tooltip and item hover as separate visual profiles.",
    "Use flat effective opaque colors for the measured item profile; do not copy Java tooltip gradient/alpha constants.",
    "Treat the step polygon as an observed-corner candidate. Recheck fractional corner coverage in browser rather than calling it certified pixel equality.",
    "Use measured10game line advance as a target. Resolve font and glyph bearing before claiming exact padding or natural width.",
    "Keep pointer/client mapping and Web cursor/focus fallback explicitly separate from unverified native positioning algorithms.",
    "Tooltip content, rarity, item name colors and optional detailed lines come from the host. An automatic Durability percentage line is not defined by hover_text_renderer JSON."
  ],
  "verificationBoundary": "A/B/C support these named source bindings, stable UI composites, local outline and text observations. They do not establish complete native whole-screen equality, every item tooltip mode, rarity palette, advanced information layout, font identity, cursor offset, clipping algorithm or internal shader state."
